[2026-03-14T21:26:49.891Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kpnt7qW9MXkHdCmGNk53h6","type":"tool_result","content":"427:#### Test: Filters toolbar renders with Status, Priority, and Label filters\n428-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues`\n429-- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays three filter controls: \"Status\" dropdown, \"Priority\" dropdown, and \"Label\" dropdown. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a multi-select dropdown.\n--\n431:#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n432-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues`\n433-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n--\n436:#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n437-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog (2), In Progress (1), Done (1)\n438-- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects only \"In Progress\"\n--\n441:#### Test: Status filter allows multi-select\n442-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog (2), In Progress (1), Done (1)\n443-- **Action**: User opens Status filter, checks \"In Progress\" and \"Done\"\n--\n446:#### Test: Priority filter dropdown shows all priorities with icons\n447-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues`\n448-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Priority\" filter button\n--\n451:#### Test: Priority filter filters issues by selected priorities\n452-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues with priorities High (2), Medium (1), Low (1)\n453-- **Action**: User opens Priority filter and selects \"High\"\n--\n456:#### Test: Label filter dropdown shows all available labels\n457-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (green), \"Improvement\" (blue)\n458-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" filter button\n--\n461:#### Test: Label filter filters issues by selected labels\n462-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 issues: ENG-1 (labeled \"Bug\"), ENG-2 (labeled \"Feature\"), ENG-3 (labeled \"Bug\", \"Feature\")\n463-- **Action**: User opens Label filter and selects \"Bug\"\n--\n466:#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n467-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues: ENG-1 (High priority, Bug label, In Progress), ENG-2 (High priority, Feature label, In Progress), ENG-3 (Low priority, Bug label, Backlog)\n468-- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter and \"Bug\" in Label filter\n--\n471:#### Test: Clearing a filter restores all issues\n472-- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\" only, showing 1 issue\n473-- **Action**: User opens Status filter and deselects \"In Progress\" (or clicks a \"Clear\" option)\n--\n476:#### Test: Filters can be used repeatedly after clearing\n477-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated with multiple issues at various statuses and priorities\n478-- **Action**: User applies Priority filter for \"High\", clears it, then applies Priority filter for \"Low\", clears it, then applies Status filter for \"Done\"\n--\n481:#### Test: Filter state shows active filter indicators\n482-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no filters applied\n483-- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter\n--\n486:#### Test: Filters persist while navigating within the page\n487-- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\", viewing filtered results\n488-- **Action**: User clicks an issue title to view detail, then navigates back to `/my-issues`\n--\n841:#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n842-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n843-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n--\n846:#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n847-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in Backlog (3), In Progress (2), Done (1)\n848-- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects only \"In Progress\"\n--\n851:#### Test: Priority filter dropdown shows all priorities with icons\n852-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n853-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Priority\" filter button\n--\n856:#### Test: Priority filter filters issues by selected priorities\n857-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with priorities High (2), Medium (1), Low (1)\n858-- **Action**: User opens Priority filter and selects \"High\"\n--\n871:#### Test: Label filter dropdown shows all available labels\n872-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (green), \"Improvement\" (blue)\n873-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" filter button\n--\n876:#### Test: Label filter filters issues by selected labels\n877-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (labeled \"Bug\"), ENG-2 (labeled \"Feature\"), ENG-3 (labeled \"Bug\", \"Feature\")\n878-- **Action**: User opens Label filter and selects \"Bug\"\n--\n901:#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n902-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues: ENG-1 (High priority, Bug label, In Progress), ENG-2 (High priority, Feature label, In Progress), ENG-3 (Low priority, Bug label, Backlog)\n903-- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter and \"Bug\" in Label filter\n--\n906:#### Test: Clearing a filter restores all issues\n907-- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\" only, showing 2 issues out of 6 total\n908-- **Action**: User opens Status filter and deselects \"In Progress\" (or clicks a \"Clear\" option)\n--\n911:#### Test: Filter state shows active filter indicators\n912-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no filters applied\n913-- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter\n--\n916:#### Test: Filters can be used repeatedly after clearing\n917-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated with multiple issues at various statuses and priorities\n918-- **Action**: User applies Priority filter for \"High\", clears it, then applies Assignee filter for \"Alice\", clears it, then applies Status filter for \"Done\"\n--\n925:#### Test: Filters persist while navigating within the page\n926-- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\", viewing filtered results\n927-- **Action**: User clicks an issue title to view detail, then navigates back to `/team/eng-1/issues`\n--\n1683:#### Test: Filters toolbar renders with Status, Lead, and Team filters\n1684-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`\n1685-- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the project list displays three filter controls: \"Status\" dropdown, \"Lead\" dropdown, and \"Team\" dropdown. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a dropdown.\n--\n1687:#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all project statuses\n1688-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`\n1689-- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n--\n1692:#### Test: Status filter filters projects by selected status\n1693-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. Projects exist: \"Auth Rewrite\" (In Progress), \"Mobile App\" (Planned), \"Bug Fixes\" (Completed).\n1694-- **Action**: User opens Status filter and selects \"In Progress\"\n--\n1697:#### Test: Status filter allows multi-select\n1698-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. Projects exist with statuses: Planned (1), In Progress (1), Completed (1).\n1699-- **Action**: User opens Status filter and checks \"Planned\" and \"In Progress\"\n--\n1722:#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n1723-- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/projects`. \"Auth Rewrite\" (In Progress, lead Alice, Engineering), \"Mobile App\" (In Progress, lead Bob, Design), \"API v2\" (Planned, lead Alice, Engineering).\n1