[2026-03-14T21:27:07.984Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019ixQN6iSZuHdP2BWNYg2fd","type":"tool_result","content":"   427→#### Test: Filters toolbar renders with Status, Priority, and Label filters\n   428→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues`\n   429→- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays three filter controls: \"Status\" dropdown, \"Priority\" dropdown, and \"Label\" dropdown. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a multi-select dropdown.\n   430→\n   431→#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n   432→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues`\n   433→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n   434→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red). Each option has a checkbox.\n   435→\n   436→#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n   437→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog (2), In Progress (1), Done (1)\n   438→- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects only \"In Progress\"\n   439→- **Expected**: Only the \"In Progress\" group is displayed with its 1 issue. Backlog and Done groups are hidden. The Status filter button shows a visual indicator that a filter is active (e.g., highlighted, badge count \"1\").\n   440→\n   441→#### Test: Status filter allows multi-select\n   442→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog (2), In Progress (1), Done (1)\n   443→- **Action**: User opens Status filter, checks \"In Progress\" and \"Done\"\n   444→- **Expected**: Both \"In Progress\" and \"Done\" groups are displayed. \"Backlog\" group is hidden. The filter button indicates 2 statuses selected.\n   445→\n   446→#### Test: Priority filter dropdown shows all priorities with icons\n   447→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues`\n   448→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Priority\" filter button\n   449→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing: Urgent (alert-triangle, red), High (arrow-up, orange), Medium (minus, yellow), Low (arrow-down, blue), No Priority (dots-horizontal, gray). Each option has a checkbox.\n   450→\n   451→#### Test: Priority filter filters issues by selected priorities\n   452→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues with priorities High (2), Medium (1), Low (1)\n   453→- **Action**: User opens Priority filter and selects \"High\"\n   454→- **Expected**: Only issues with High priority are displayed across all status groups. Issues with Medium and Low priority are hidden.\n   455→\n   456→#### Test: Label filter dropdown shows all available labels\n   457→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (green), \"Improvement\" (blue)\n   458→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" filter button\n   459→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all workspace labels with their colored dots and names. Each option has a checkbox.\n   460→\n   461→#### Test: Label filter filters issues by selected labels\n   462→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 issues: ENG-1 (labeled \"Bug\"), ENG-2 (labeled \"Feature\"), ENG-3 (labeled \"Bug\", \"Feature\")\n   463→- **Action**: User opens Label filter and selects \"Bug\"\n   464→- **Expected**: Only issues with the \"Bug\" label are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-3). ENG-2 is hidden.\n   465→\n   466→#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n   467→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues: ENG-1 (High priority, Bug label, In Progress), ENG-2 (High priority, Feature label, In Progress), ENG-3 (Low priority, Bug label, Backlog)\n   468→- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter and \"Bug\" in Label filter\n   469→- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 is shown (it matches both High priority AND Bug label). ENG-2 and ENG-3 are hidden.\n   470→\n   471→#### Test: Clearing a filter restores all issues\n   472→- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\" only, showing 1 issue\n   473→- **Action**: User opens Status filter and deselects \"In Progress\" (or clicks a \"Clear\" option)\n   474→- **Expected**: All issues are shown again across all status groups, same as the unfiltered view.\n   475→\n   476→#### Test: Filters can be used repeatedly after clearing\n   477→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated with multiple issues at various statuses and priorities\n   478→- **Action**: User applies Priority filter for \"High\", clears it, then applies Priority filter for \"Low\", clears it, then applies Status filter for \"Done\"\n   479→- **Expected**: Each filter application and clearing works correctly. After the final action, only \"Done\" issues are shown. Filters remain responsive and functional through multiple interactions.\n   480→\n   481→#### Test: Filter state shows active filter indicators\n   482→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no filters applied\n   483→- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter\n   484→- **Expected**: The Priority filter button shows a visual indicator that it is active (e.g., highlighted background, badge showing \"1\", or different styling). Status and Label filter buttons remain in their default/inactive state.\n   485→\n   486→#### Test: Filters persist while navigating within the page\n   487→- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\", viewing filtered results\n   488→- **Action**: User clicks an issue title to view detail, then navigates back to `/my-issues`\n   489→- **Expected**: The filters are still applied showing only \"In Progress\" issues. The filter state is preserved across navigation.\n   490→\n   491→## Inbox Page (`/inbox`)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3553acc8-e37d-492f-a872-c9b8ee782554","uuid":"b056dc9f-5aef-4e6c-860c-748685170180","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md","content":"#### Test: Filters toolbar renders with Status, Priority, and Label filters\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues`\n- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays three filter controls: \"Status\" dropdown, \"Priority\" dropdown, and \"Label\" dropdown. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a multi-select dropdown.\n\n#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red). Each option has a checkbox.\n\n#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog (2), In Progress (1), Done (1)\n- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects only \"In Progress\"\n- **Expected**: Only the \"In Progress\" group is displayed with its 1 issue. Backlog and Done groups are hidden. The Status filter button shows a visual indicator that a filter is active (e.g., highlighted, badge count \"1\").\n\n#### Test: Status filter allows multi-select\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog (2), In Progress (1), Done (1)\n- **Action**: User opens Status filter, checks \"In Progress\" and \"Done\"\n- **Expected**: Both \"In Progress\" and \"Done\" groups are displayed. \"Backlog\" group is hidden. The filter button indicates 2 statuses selected.\n\n#### Test: Priority filter dropdown shows all priorities with icons\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues`\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Priority\" filter button\n- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing: Urgent (alert-triangle, red), High (arrow-up, orange), Medium (minus, yellow), Low (arrow-down, blue), No Priority (dots-horizontal, gray). Each option has a checkbox.\n\n#### Test: Priority filter filters issues by selected priorities\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues with priorities High (2), Medium (1), Low (1)\n- **Action**: User opens Priority filter and selects \"High\"\n- **Expected**: Only issues with High priority are displayed across all status groups. Issues with Medium and Low priority are hidden.\n\n#### Test: Label filter dropdown shows all available labels\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has labels \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (green), \"Improvement\" (blue)\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Label\" filter button\n- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all workspace labels with their colored dots and names. Each option has a checkbox.\n\n#### Test: Label filter filters issues by selected labels\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 issues: ENG-1 (labeled \"Bug\"), ENG-2 (labeled \"Feature\"), ENG-3 (labeled \"Bug\", \"Feature\")\n- **Action**: User opens Label filter and selects \"Bug\"\n- **Expected**: Only issues with the \"Bug\" label are shown (ENG-1 and ENG-3). ENG-2 is hidden.\n\n#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues: ENG-1 (High priority, Bug label, In Progress), ENG-2 (High priority, Feature label, In Progress), ENG-3 (Low priority, Bug label, Backlog)\n- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter and \"Bug\" in Label filter\n- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 is shown (it matches both High priority AND Bug label). ENG-2 and ENG-3 are hidden.\n\n#### Test: Clearing a filter restores all issues\n- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\" only, showing 1 issue\n- **Action**: User opens Status filter and deselects \"In Progress\" (or clicks a \"Clear\" option)\n- **Expected**: All issues are shown again across all status groups, same as the unfiltered view.\n\n#### Test: Filters can be used repeatedly after clearing\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated with multiple issues at various statuses and priorities\n- **Action**: User applies Priority filter for \"High\", clears it, then applies Priority filter for \"Low\", clears it, then applies Status filter for \"Done\"\n- **Expected**: Each filter application and clearing works correctly. After the final action, only \"Done\" issues are shown. Filters remain responsive and functional through multiple interactions.\n\n#### Test: Filter state shows active filter indicators\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, no filters applied\n- **Action**: User selects \"High\" in Priority filter\n- **Expected**: The Priority filter button shows a visual indicator that it is active (e.g., highlighted background, badge showing \"1\", or different styling). Status and Label filter buttons remain in their default/inactive state.\n\n#### Test: Filters persist while navigating within the page\n- **Initial state**: User has Status filter set to \"In Progress\", viewing filtered results\n- **Action**: User clicks an issue title to view detail, then navigates back to `/my-issues`\n- **Expected**: The filters are still applied showing only \"In Progress\" issues. The filter state is preserved across navigation.\n\n## Inbox Page (`/inbox`)","numLines":65,"startLine":427,"totalLines":2686}}}
